 "notes": "De Kuilen at Langenboom near Mill: the beach entry on the north-west shore below the Fazantenweg car park (the OpenStreetMap dive-site node) and the fossil sea-floor layer in the south-east corner; shoreline and beaches from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). The site is named only 'Mill'; De Kuilen is the dive site at Mill, so it is assumed to be here. From the entry, about 50 m out the bottom reaches depth, and a heading of 90 degrees leads over a planted slope into peat walls, canyons and craters down to 35 m; the fossil layer (8-50 cm thick) is placed only by 'south-east corner', and the walls are not drawn because their positions are not known. The site coordinates are Mill village centre, about 3 km south-east of the lake.",
